    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in the service layer, where owner creation actually completes.\n\nIn `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) \u2014 the exact name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches its appender to.\n2. In `saveOwner(owner, sharesHousehold)`, captured `owner.isNew()` into `isCreate` **before** saving (after `save()`, the entity has an id and is no longer \"new\").\n3. After a successful `ownerRepository.save(owner)`, emit a single audit line **only on create**, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```\n   AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-01\n   ```\n\nPlacing it in `saveOwner` (rather than the controller) ensures the line is emitted after the create-time fields (`customerCode`, `registrationDate`) are populated and the id is assigned, and that it fires only for creates \u2014 not updates, which call the same method. The test confirms the emitted line contains the id, customerCode, and registrationDate returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
